    "title": {
      "en": "Geometric Progression (GP) and its sum"
    },
    "blocks": [
      {
        "id": "story",
        "type": "story",
        "provenance": "original",
        "title": {
          "en": "The bouncing ball"
        },
        "text": {
          "en": "A ball dropped from 64 cm rebounds to half its previous height each time: 64, 32, 16, 8 ... Here we multiply by the same number each time instead of adding."
        }
      },
      {
        "id": "explain",
        "type": "explanation",
        "provenance": "original",
        "keepEnglishTerms": [
          "GP",
          "common ratio r",
          "a, ar, ar^2",
          "t_n = a r^(n-1)",
          "b^2 = ac",
          "S_n",
          "r = 1"
        ],
        "text": {
          "en": "A sequence in which each term is obtained by multiplying the previous term by a fixed non-zero number r is a Geometric Progression (GP).\nThe fixed multiplier r is the common ratio: r = t2 / t1 = t3 / t2.\nA GP with first term a is a, ar, ar squared, ar cubed, ...\nThe n-th term is t_n = a r^(n-1).\nThree non-zero numbers a, b, c are in GP exactly when b squared = ac.\nThe sum of n terms is S_n = a (r^n - 1)/(r - 1) when r is greater than 1, and S_n = a (1 - r^n)/(1 - r) when r is less than 1.\nIf r = 1 then S_n = n x a."
        }
      },
